### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Run "Send Request" above each block.
@base = http://localhost:5000/api
@guest = 11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Create a text file as a guest
POST {{base}}/docs
x-guest-id: {{guest}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "hello.txt", "content": "Hello from the API" }

### List files
GET {{base}}/docs?sort=name&limit=10
x-guest-id: {{guest}}

### Dashboard numbers
GET {{base}}/stats
x-guest-id: {{guest}}

### Register (keeps the guest's files)
# @name register
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test User", "email": "test@example.com", "password": "secret123", "guestId": "{{guest}}" }

### Login (demo user from `npm run seed`)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@uniview.app", "password": "Demo@1234" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Who am I
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Folders
GET {{base}}/folders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search
GET {{base}}/search?q=plan
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
